new file mode 100644
index 0000000..84c998a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+# smallpt — A little light experiment
+
+Kevin Beason's smallpt C++ path tracer, compiled to WebAssembly with Emscripten. Open `index.html` through an HTTP server (`npm start`). All runtime rendering happens client-side in a module Web Worker; no rendering service or GPU is needed.
+
+The page starts a progressive render automatically. Randomize changes both sphere colors and the side walls and starts a new render. Resolution and sample controls also rerender; pause/resume, original-scene reset, fullscreen, and PNG export are available.
+
+## Build
+
+Install Emscripten and put `em++` on PATH, then run:
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+npm test
+```
+
+Compiled `public/smallpt.js` and `public/smallpt.wasm` are checked in, so serving the site does not require a compiler. `npm test` executes the browser-targeted Wasm artifact in a Node harness and checks nonempty output, opacity, color changes, repeatability, and reset. No browser automation is required.
+
+`src/smallpt-original.cpp` is the unchanged upstream renderer, downloaded from https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/smallpt.cpp. The bridge in `src/renderer.cpp` replaces the command-line entry point with a progressive framebuffer API, preserving the original radiance function, camera, materials, 2×2 subpixel sampling, and scene geometry. Color accumulation occurs independently for each subpixel before clamping and gamma conversion. Each pass adds four samples per pixel.
+
+`public/preview.png` is a 128-sample render generated from that same C++ bridge. It appears while the Wasm module initializes and is replaced by the live render after the first complete pass.
+
+Original code: Copyright © 2008 Kevin Beason, MIT license (see `src/LICENSE.smallpt.txt`).
